  "description": "Tree: 1 No. London Plane (Platanus ? acerifolia)\rTree location - The Old Deanery, Deans Court, London, EC4V 5AA\r\rThe proposed works comprise selective crown reduction and pruning to provide clearance from the adjacent building and facilitate the planned construction works and crane access.\r\rThe existing crown spread towards each elevation in meters measures\rCreed Lane ? 6.8m\rLudgate Hill 10.8m\rThe proposed remaining crown spread in metres.\rCreed Lane 2.2m\rLudgate Hill 4.6m\rThe length of live crown to be removed.\rCreed Lane 4m\rLudgate Hill 6.2m\rApproximate maximum diameter of the branches likely to be removed in centimetres - 15cm\rProposed finished clearance between the crown and building in meters.\rCreed Lane 0m\rLudgate Hill 6.2m\r\rThe reductions will be achieved through selective removal of suitable branches and branch sections, with pruning cuts made at appropriate pruning points. The works will seek to retain a balanced and natural crown form while maintaining the health and structural integrity of the tree.\r\rAny dead, damaged, diseased or otherwise unsuitable branches identified during the works may also be removed where appropriate.\r\rThe works are required to provide the necessary clearance from the building to facilitate construction activities and crane operations, while retaining the tree in a safe, healthy and structurally appropriate condition.\r\rAll works will be undertaken by competent arboricultural operatives in accordance with the accompanying RAMS and good arboricultural practice. Larger branches will be lowered in a controlled manner using suitable arboricultural rigging equipment where required.",
